      "index": 3,
      "kind": "cycle-1-answer",
      "content": "\n\nThe `docs/interactive-serving.md` document describes how MIInfer's experimental interactive serving mode works on gfx906 hardware. The key behaviors include:\n\n**Presets:** Two presets exist \u2014 `m25_hi_qualified` for P512 benchmarking, and `m25_interactive` which adds wide-prefill MX repacked attention decode flags (`MIINFER_MX_MMV=1`, `MIINFER_PREFILL_WIDE_MX_REPACKED_ATTN_DECODE=1`) to enable a more capable serving configuration (lines 3\u20136).\n\n**Wide prefill chunking:** Long prompts are processed in bounded offset-aware chunks rather than one monolithic pass. For example, 3991 tokens become \"7 x 512 + 384 + 23\" chunks, while attention KV, recurrent state, and convolution history persist across those chunks so numerical results remain consistent with a single-pass execution (lines 19\u201321).\n\n**Session reuse / checkpoint cache:** When enabled via `MIINFER_SESSION_REUSE=1`, the server keeps up to eight GPU checkpoints at sparse 512-token boundaries within a 3 GiB cap.",
      "reasoning_content": "\n\n",
